---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('012-treachery', 'chapter-3')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Welcome to Chapter 3 - finally some plot development for the overarcing story! Read on...\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Greatest_Attack_Call_Ever\">The Greatest Attack Call Ever</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Greatest Attack Call Ever\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_3?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Greatest Attack Call Ever\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>New chapter means new character of course!\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><span class=\"new\" title=\"Laguna Loire/Dissidia (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTGFndW5hX0xvaXJlL0Rpc3NpZGlhP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Laguna</span></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/04/Laguna012.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110410151924\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Laguna012\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/04/Laguna012.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/84?cb=20110410151924\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"84\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Laguna012.PNG\" data-image-key=\"Laguna012.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Ah, Laguna. I wasn't too big on him in FF8, he was a goof and a half-insane loon, like most of the cast of that game come to think of it. Dissidia however has made him one hell of a badass, giving him an unrivaled arsenal of weaponry and tweaking his quirks to be genuinely funny. Laguna is a well-meaning do-gooder who just has a habit of misusing words and getting confused when it comes to directions. Also give a big round of applause for his VA, A.V. Kennedy, who does an awesome job, especially since it's his first time with SE voicing a character who has never been voiced by anyone before. He turns in what I consider one of the more memorable and character-fitting performances alongside Kefka, Kain and The Emperor.\n</p><p>Laguna is far and away the hardest of the new six to use, relying on tactical fighting and pressuring the opponent to catch them when they slip or or trap them between two attacks to inflict pain. His Bravery attacks hurt a lot but are easy to block, but that's where the trickery on your part comes in. Laguna's HP attacks are slow to use but combo well with his Bravery attacks. For example, throw a Sticky Bomb at the opponent, then call down a Satellite Beam as it explodes so they can't dodge, or fire out a Homing Bazooka missile and smack the opponent in the face with Ragnarok Blade as they try to dodge the missile. Or, flip it around. You get the point. This makes Laguna very hard to use and he'll require practice, fortunately you have an Assist the entire storyline as a crutch if his slow HP attacks are giving you trouble.\n</p><p>He starts off with some of his key attacks, Machine Gun and Missile Barrage. Machine Gun is just a solid attack option that does a lot of damage, and Missile Barrage fires out six missiles that turn and weave to track enemies, and should be used to combo with Satellite Beam or Ragnarok Blade as mentioned above. He'll quickly learn the Ricochet Shot attack, letting him shoot a bullet off of obstacles to bounce the shrapnel into an enemy, and he picks up Ragnarok Blaster as an HP attack, blasting the enemy on the ground at close-range. Once you master him Laguna is quite effective and hurts a lot, but it will require effort. And of course, his EX Burst makes it worthwhile too.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>As you suit Laguna up before beginning the story, I did some quick math and found out the Power Ring with a 1.5 booster and a Red Drop is stronger than the Ring with two boosters, so yeah, let's go with that build from now on. He won't have a weapon unless you wanna buy him one, but don't, he'll be tough enough to handle the enemies we meet as we begin and before we exit the starting gateway we'll find a weapon for him for free. And alas, while the shop may have new wares, none of them are the Altair. The Capella remains out of our reach for a while longer...\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Tanegashima\"><img alt=\"Tanegashima\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fleeting Flash\"><img alt=\"Fleeting Flash\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Wraith\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Cross Chain\"><img alt=\"Cross Chain\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Vision\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Vision\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fleeting Flash\"><img alt=\"Fleeting Flash\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>We'll quickly see that as goofy as he acts, Laguna knows a strategy when it hits him in the face. The first chest gives us a Cross Chain, and Laguna lets us know precisely where to use it - C4, of course, chains all five enemies for a cool 25 KP. The enemies of this stage are NEW! Yes, gone are the Idle Sky Pirates and Delusory Dragoons, my comrades! We instead have two Fleeting Flashs, a Counterfeit Wraith, a Transient Gunner, and an Ephemeral Vision. \n</p><p>The Wraith has an Anti-Air Particle Beam attack that fires four lasers high in the air in a square formation around her, and she moves towards you on start-up, it has weak horizontal range for a back-dodge will be enough to avoid it. She also has two Tentacle Moves with varying effects, the ground one has her use a spin attack you can't block, and at full charge fires a large energy orb you can reflect to damage her. The aerial tentacle blow fires several energy orbs at us that bounce along the ground and are easily avoided by being airborne. The Gunner has the same moves you have and will be fought last so you'll know how to handle it by that point. The Vision has Hop Step on the ground, a quick and hard-to-anticipate move, fortunately it has low range, and in the air uses Dart &amp; Weave, where he dodges our attack and jumps up to come down spinning. Fortunately if he uses it when we aren't attacking it's ridiculously easy to block and punish. The HP attack is Energy Rain, when you see the notice appear run away because he'll bounce off you, even stopping attacks, and bombards you with magic blasts.\n</p><p>Being that the enemies are dumb, don't worry about comboing Laguna's moves too much, just Machine Gun or Shotgun them and then slam them with a Ragnarok Blade or Satellite Beam. Open the chest when you're done mopping up the opposition to find a Tanegashima, a gun-type weapon that of course Laguna can use, so let him. It also unlocks the Valiant in the shop, not as badass as the Capella but still nice, but we lack a Fish Scale and won't have one for a while so too bad. That's the main problem with D012's shop, by the time you can access trade accessories consistently the equipment you need them to trade for are underpowered compared to the point in the story you'll be at, but you have to take them anyway to unlock higher-level equipment, which you'll also lack the trade accessories to get, and so on until you get to the top Level 100 equipment. Yup, you'll find that a good half or so of the cost of most equipment pieces you'll be buying is actually spent paying for lower-level equipment pieces you need so you can trade up to what you actually wanted in the first place - like how we want an Altair right now just so we can get the Capella. Squiggly-mouth emoticon,&#160;:/.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Exploration\">Exploration</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Exploration\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_3?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Exploration\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Laguna is one the world map now, the music is a remix of Eyes on Me, insufferable in FF8 but here as a world map theme with no lyrics, actually quite nice. Immediately turn around to explore the region behind us, there's a blue gateway between a ring of grass, and a chest by the closed gateway near it with a KP Gambler. Save this item, it is very useful later and will make big bucks for us. The Phantasmal Harlequin outside the gateway has no new tricks to watch for. To the left of the gateway is a stone that produces a grind bar leading to an island with our fourth Pink Tail. Head for the gateway now.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Fish Scale\"><img alt=\"Fish Scale\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<t