t-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/be/Dissicon_ff12_Vaan1.png/revision/latest?cb=20110126022706\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Vaan - Assist\"><img alt=\"Vaan - Assist\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"31\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff12 Vaan1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff12_Vaan1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/be/Dissicon_ff12_Vaan1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/31?cb=20110126022706\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Enemy Name\"><img alt=\"Enemy Name\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Gunner\"><img alt=\"Transient Gunner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Use a Cross Chain at C3 to get all the enemies, good time for that EX Charge. Let's chat about Laguna's EX Mode while I bring it up. His special bonus is to instantly cancel out the lag from a Bravery attack by using another one, letting him launch even more firepower than ever. His EX Burst is actually pretty challenging to get right, you have to hold R and move the cursor to center the opponent between a crosshair as they move around, and if you land enough hits to fill up the power bar Laguna summons his hyperspace arsenal together to charge power and fire a giant laser cannon...which he rides. Badass? Very. And it comes complete with the best attack call of any video game ever. I'll let you hear for yourself so as to not ruin the fun.\n</p><p>The enemy line-up is two each Sky Pirates, Wraiths and Gunners. This time around the Wraith is the Strange Battle Piece and is packing Mandragora. Her HP attack is pretty nasty, 0-Form Particle Beam, she charges for a second and then fires a big laser beam a short distance, turning to track you if you dodge. It's very difficult to avoid at close-range, when she begins to charge it up run away and then dodge backwards when it fires. You can slam her with an HP attack as she recovers, so it's not hard to win. Otherwise, nothing new here to watch for. The Cross Chain at C3 will miss the Sky Pirate at E4, you'll have to fight him after. As I fought Laguna got to Level 15 and learned Pummel and Sticky Bomb. Pummel is an effective two-hit keep-away attack and is handy in his aerial arsenal when he learns the midair version, but for now his current line-up of ground attacks is fine. Sticky Bomb throws an explosive that sticks to the opponent and explodes several seconds later, great for comboing with other attacks but it's easy to block so it's hard to use, but you might as well if you've got the CP.\n</p><p>The new Summonstone is Carbuncle, it summons when our Bravery hits 0 - probably after landing an HP hit - and mirrors the opponent's Bravery to 0. For now it's useless, oh it'll be effective down the road, but at this point by the time you're going for an HP hit, it's probably after the opponent is already Broken so Carbuncle will do nothing, and we also have Cactuar which is just as effective for sapping the opponent's power, and can be called whenever we like. When you approach the path to the end piece, Vaan vanishes, so we'll be fighting the boss alone. Laguna finds himself alone in the World of Darkness, when suddenly, something stripperific this way comes.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Cloud_of_Darkness_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Cloud of Darkness (Dissidia PSP)\">Cloud of Darkness</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/46/CoDDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110228054507\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"CoDDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"137\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"CoDDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"CoDDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/46/CoDDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/137?cb=20110228054507\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">2,446\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">12\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">261\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Tentacle of Scorn, Tentacle of Pain, Tentacle of Spite, Tentacle of Suffering\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Wide-Angle Particle Beam, Anti-Air Particle Beam, Aura Ball, Fusillade Particle Beam, 0-Form Particle Beam\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Iron Giant\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1.5/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The Cloud of Darkness has all four tentacle attacks, whose effects including to recap - ground variants which create dark electricity around you, send a large orb of darkness forward, spin attack, or just lash out to strike you, and aerial variants which fire two dark energy balls, fire a swarm of smaller ones, whirl to attack in a sphere, or lash out. She has two new HP attacks. Wide-Angle Particle Beam has a second of charge before a wave of dark energy appears with a wide horizontal range and sweeps forward quickly, not too hard to dodge if you see it coming. Aura Ball creates several large spheres of darkness one by one that spread out and move towards you, then explode when she wills it. Overall a pretty versatile pool of HP attacks to trip you up with, and her tentacles are hard to predict too.\n</p><p>What breaks this fight through and stops a potential 2 or even 3 on the scale is one problem for her - Ifrit. I Broke her with a single Ricochet Shot, and Ifrit then boosted me to 1600 Bravery, Wall Rush her and a good 2000 HP of hers vanishes in the first 15 seconds of the fight. After that mopping her up was pretty simple, and while she can be a difficult fight if you're a beginner, the ability to take off 2000 HP so easily will swing the fight your way regardless of skill level, if you've made it this far there's no reason you can't handle her.\n</p><p>In the aftermath of the scene, Laguna suddenly notices the Cloud of Darkness is hot, and suddenly gets a leg cramp. The Cloud of Darkness, understandably dumbfounded by this, has a chat with him when he mentions he's fighting not for Cosmos but just to go home. She tells him where the Manikins came from and how to stop them from increasing their numbers, by closing the portal they're using to emerge from the Rift. And why tell him this? Because she wants to see how he handles it, it would be a suicide mission to seek out the portal, so what will Laguna do? She overestimated his dumb heroicness. Laguna heads off and that ends the chapter. Unlike the last two, no Reports this time.\n</p><p>As always, main menu for Mognet and to buy some PP Catalog calendar upgrades. \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</strong> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\"